  "recipe": {
    "method": "tools/audio_cues.py build --downloads .local/audio-downloads: per variation, an ffmpeg mix of the layers in recipe.json (trim, tape-style pitch, high/low-pass, fades, gain, placement) to 48 kHz mono, a look-ahead limiter of at most the category's limit_db (or the cue's own limit_db), one gain to the category's integrated loudness capped at -1 dBTP, then triangular dither to 16-bit PCM",
    "approved_reference": "Ticket #243 on spec #239's tone brief (as #242): dark high fantasy; the spend cues are quiet leather, glass, liquid and a low growl under the action's own sound; protection is a ringing steel ward; a round is a bell and a drum; the finale a longer brass arpeggio and chord with gong and bell tree; the run's end a low bell tolled twice over a tuba drone",
